description.narrative:
Output: 1. Component 1 - Construction of Middle Marshyangdi- Marshyangdi 132 kV line, Butwal-Kohalpur 132 kV line second circuit, and Chapali grid substation; expansion of Matatirtha grid sublstation; and installation of capacitor banks;
2. Component 2 - Construction of eight primary distribution  substations and three distribution switching stations;

3. Component 3 - Rehabilitation of Marshyandi and Gandak hydropower stations;
4. Component 4 - Rebuilding of of 11kV feeders, relevant low-voltage networks, and associated facilities in pilot areas;
5. Component 5 - Countrywide expansion of the CFL program;
6. Component 6 - Establishment of solar/solar-wind street lighting systems;
7. Component 7 - Introduction of PPP in distribution and Implementation support for component 4 
Indicator: 132 kV transmission line length increased by 248 km and grid substation capacity increased by 80 MVA 
Progress/Status: Stringing of 232 km transmission line out of 280 km completed. Butwal-Kohalpur section is energized. 150 MVA capacity of S/S installation completed and charged. Contract for  Package A1 has been terminated by NEA. Contract variation of SCADA under Package A2 has been done.A 22.5 MVA power transformer (Package A8) encountered problem during charging at Parwanipur, which is being repaired. 
Data Source: Quarterly progress reports
Reports of review missions
Project completion report 
